ity and since it was only  meant for him  it closes at his death  so what  my idea which your tweet sparked  is a seeker of truth  can never gain enlightenment from  another or ask permission of another or  bribe another or ask another to  enlighten  him or her  because that's something that cannot be  given by another  it can only be earned by the seeker  themselves  the door was always open until the time  of the man's death at which time  the door was closed and locked forever  the man was looking for instructions  for prescriptions on 10 ways to walk  through the door of justice he was  seeking a weigh-in but asking all the  wrong questions he was stopped by his  own reality tunnel belief system  that told him he must follow the rules  of social convention perforce of others  to get through the door  when if he realizes that life is a  single-player game he would have ignored  by failing to understand that life is a  single-player game he adhered to game  rules or social conventions and beliefs  which forever blocked him from going  through the open door  because he conflated consensus reality  with his own reality leading him to all  the grown paths  you must simply walk through it  the door of the law  or the gateless gate  on your own  this story appears at the end of the  book the trial which was written by  franz kafka now two quotes that comes to  my mind when thinking about this story  you enter the forest at the darkest  point where there is no path  where there is a way or path  is someone else's path  you are not on your own path if you  follow someone else's way  you are not going to realize your full  potential by joseph campbell judge man  by his questions not his answers  voltaire and now i leave you with some  words from kapil gupta and navarro kant  who also shed some light on this matter  if you want to be the best in the world  at anything you cannot follow  prescription if you want to be okay at  it then sure you can follow a  prescription if 